# Code owners. Installed from docs/spec/factory/.github/CODEOWNERS, with the team set and the paths of the
# specification bundle pointed at docs/spec/, where it is kept in this repository.
#
# Branch rules require a code owner's approving review for a pull request that touches any path below
# (ADR-0023, ADR-0029). Everything else merges on the factory's checks: tier low and medium automatically,
# tier high after `factory/human-approval`.
#
# The team must contain humans only: no app, no bot, no machine user, and it needs write access to this
# repository or GitHub ignores the entries. An approving review is the one thing an agent cannot produce.
#
# Keep this list in step with `sensitivePaths` in docs/spec/factory/.github/factory/policy.json. The policy is
# wider on purpose: it also makes paths tier high that need a human review without needing a code OWNER
# (Directory.Packages.props and .editorconfig: a change the plan declared is tier medium, a patch update to
# Directory.Packages.props must be able to merge automatically, and any other change to either is tier high; ADR-0034).

# What is to be built, and the decisions: the specification bundle (spec, ADRs, agent guidance,
# the factory kit with its live policy and gate scripts) and feature specs
/docs/spec/                                @wtf-corp/admins
/specs/**/spec.md                          @wtf-corp/admins
/specs/0000-framework/                     @wtf-corp/admins
/adr/                                      @wtf-corp/admins

